1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,860
A Fair Competition.
公平竞赛。

2
00:00:03,860 --> 00:00:34,520
Swifter, Higher and Stronger stands for the spirit of the Olympics. But fairness is the basis of this motto. Only when you win fairly will you and your homeland deserve the great glory.
“更快、更高、更强”代表着奥林匹克精神。但公平是这句格言的基础。只有公平地赢得比赛，你和你的祖国才配得上这份荣耀。

3
00:00:34,520 --> 00:01:38,213
But nowadays, unlike the ancient honest slave competitors, some hopeless athletes who can’t bear the pain of training cheat when taking part in games. Medals seem to have magical power causing them to cheat, and the prize money has replaced the motto as their only goal. So, in the gymnastics event to be held in our city next month, one of the host’s responsibilities is to keep competitions fair.
但如今，与古代诚实的奴隶选手不同，某些没有出息的运动员无法忍受训练的痛苦，参加比赛时便作弊。奖牌似乎有一种魔力，驱使他们作弊，奖金也取代了格言，成了他们唯一的目标。因此，在下个月于本市举行的体操赛事中，主办方的一项责任就是保证比赛公平。

4
00:01:38,213 --> 00:02:17,640
They advertised on posters outside the stadium to promise that every competitor is to have a regular physical examination in a gymnasium one after another. No one can bargain on this. The volunteers in charge will be very strict.
他们在体育场外张贴海报，承诺每一位参赛者，都要在体育馆接受常规身体检查，一个接一个地接受检查。任何人都不能对此讨价还价。负责此事的志愿者会十分严格。

5
00:02:17,640 --> 00:02:30,733
It is foolish to cheat because they will not be admitted to compete and will even be fined as well.
作弊是愚蠢的，因为作弊者不会被允许参赛，甚至还会被罚款。
